{"Inconsistent metric tag key: `\"shards\"` here vs `\"shard\"` used by the other two metrics in this method. This will cause the `wait_produce` metric to be grouped under a different tag in dashboards.": 0.9392363429069519, "`isinstance(process, multiprocessing.Process)` is always `False` for `SpawnProcess` objects created by `get_context(\"spawn\")`. `SpawnProcess` inherits from `BaseProcess`, not `multiprocessing.Process`. This means unhealthy processes are never actually killed, and processes are never terminated during `join()`. Use `not isinstance(process, threading.Thread)` or `isinstance(process, multiprocessing.process.BaseProcess)` instead.": 0.880279541015625, "`time.sleep(0.1)` is a no-op here because `time.sleep` was already monkeypatched to `lambda _: None` at the top of this test. The flusher threads won't actually get any time to process. Save a reference to the real `sleep` before patching.": 0.9862408638000488, "`break` on deadline exits the loop entirely, skipping `terminate()` for all remaining processes. Consider using `continue` to skip waiting but still call `terminate()`, or add a cleanup loop after the `break` to terminate remaining processes.": 0.9655168056488037, "`_create_process_for_shard` (singular) is defined but never called anywhere. Only `_create_process_for_shards` (plural) is used. This is dead code that should be removed or integrated.": 0.6888095140457153}